         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>secondAVWeight</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="5" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_6">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Magic Skill:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>skill</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="7" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_8">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Associated Item 1:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>assocItem1</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="11" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_12">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Perk to Apply:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>perkToApply</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="4" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_5">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Delivery:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>delivery</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="8" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_9">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Associated Item 2:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>assocItem2</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="2" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_3">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Archetype:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>archetype</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="0" column="1">
        <widget class="QLineEdit" name="editorID"/>
       </item>
       <item row="1" column="1">
        <widget class="QLineEdit" name="name"/>
       </item>
       <item row="2" column="1">
        <widget class="QComboBox" name="archetype"/>
       </item>
       <item row="3" column="1">
        <widget class="QComboBox" name="castingType">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>&lt;p&gt;The casting type controls how the caster triggers the effect. All of the effects on a Spell or Enchantment must have the same casting type.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;dl&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;Concentration&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;&lt;p&gt;The effect is cast continuously (i.e. for as long as the player holds the &quot;cast&quot; button), draining magicka while active.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/dd&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;Fire and Forget&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;&lt;p&gt;The effect must charge, and fires once released.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/dd&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;Constant Effect&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;&lt;p&gt;The effect behaves like an ability and is always active. This only works for effects that are attached to Armor Enchantments or Ability Spells.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/dd&gt;
&lt;/dl&gt;</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="4" column="1">
        <widget class="QComboBox" name="delivery">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>&lt;p&gt;The delivery type controls how the effect is delivered to the target. All effects attached to a Spell or Enchantment must have the same delivery type.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;dl&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;Self&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;&lt;p&gt;The effect is applied to the caster.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/dd&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;Contact&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;&lt;p&gt;The effect is applied to the target by contact (a hit event). This only works for Weapon Enchantments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/dd&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;Aimed&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;&lt;p&gt;The effect is attached to a projectile, and is applied to any valid target that the projectile hits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/dd&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;Target Actor&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;&lt;p&gt;The effect is immediately applied to the actor that the caster is aiming at, without any projectile being fired. (You could think of this as being &quot;hitscan.&quot;) Note that the third-person crosshair isn't accurate, so Target Actor effects are hard for players to use at a distance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/dd&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;Target Location&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;&lt;p&gt;The effect is applied to to the object or landscape that the caster is aiming at, without any projectile being fired. (You could think of this as being &quot;hitscan.&quot;)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/dd&gt;
&lt;/dl&gt;</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="7" column="1">
        <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="assocItem1">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>One of the parameters associated with the effect and its archetype.</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="8" column="1">
        <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="assocItem2">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>One of the parameters associated with the effect and its archetype.</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="9" column="1" alignment="Qt::AlignLeft">
        <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="secondAVWeight">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>A multiplier applied to the effect's magnitude, influencing how the effect affects Associated Item 2. This is used with the Dual Value Multiplier archetype.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignRight|Qt::AlignTrailing|Qt::AlignVCenter</set>
         </property>
         <property name="decimals">
          <number>4</number>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="11" column="1">
        <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="perkToApply">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>When this effect is applied to the player, a Perk can be temporarily added to the player, to be removed when the effect ceases to apply. This does not work on NPCs, as NPCs cannot have perks added or removed dynamically during play.</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="6" column="1" alignment="Qt::AlignLeft">
        <widget class="QSpinBox" name="minSkill">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>NPCs can only use spells which contain this effect if their skill level (for the effect's magic skill) is greater than or equal to this value. This value also influences the level displayed for the effect in the Magic menu (e.g. a skill level of 25 displays as an &quot;Apprentice&quot;-level effect, but doesn't prevent lower-level players from using the effect anyway).</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignRight|Qt::AlignTrailing|Qt::AlignVCenter</set>
         </property>
         <property name="maximum">
          <number>100</number>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="5" column="1">
        <widget class="QComboBox" name="skill">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>The skill associated with the effect. The caster's skill level can influence the power, duration, or cost of the effect, and the player will gain experience in that skill when successfully casting this effect.</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="10" column="1">
        <widget class="QComboBox" name="resistAV">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>An Actor Value: the type of resistance (e.g. damage resistance, fire resistance, poison resistance) that applies to this effect. This is only used if this effect is flagged as Hostile.</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
      </layout>
     </item>
     <item>
      <layout class="QGridLayout" name="metricsLayout">
       <item row="0" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_13">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Taper Duration:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>taperDuration</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="1" column="1">
        <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="taperWeight">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>A multiplier applied to the effect's strength at the beginning of its taper duration. For example, a value of 0.5 will make the effect's strength drop by half the instant its duration elapses.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignRight|Qt::AlignTrailing|Qt::AlignVCenter</set>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="2" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_15">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Taper Curve</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>taperCurve</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="0" column="2">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_16">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Base Cost:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>baseCost</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="0" column="1">
        <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="taperDuration">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>The length of time, in seconds, for which the effect continues to affect the target after its duration has elapsed. This can be used in combination with the other &quot;Taper&quot; settings to have the effect wear off gradually rather than instantly.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignRight|Qt::AlignTrailing|Qt::AlignVCenter</set>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="1" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_14">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Taper Weight:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>taperWeight</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="1" column="2">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_17">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Skill Usage Mult:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>skillUsageMult</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="2" column="1">
        <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="taperCurve">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>&lt;p&gt;This controls how quickly the effect magnitude decreases during the taper duration. (Negative values cause the effect magnitude to increase.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is applied as an exponent. Let &lt;var&gt;M&lt;/var&gt; be the base magnitude, &lt;var&gt;W&lt;/var&gt; the Taper Weight, &lt;var&gt;D&lt;/var&gt; the Taper Duration, and &lt;var&gt;C&lt;/var&gt; the Taper Curve. At some time &lt;var&gt;t&lt;/var&gt;, the effect's magnitude is &lt;var&gt;M&lt;/var&gt;&lt;var&gt;W&lt;/var&gt; × (1 - (&lt;var&gt;t&lt;/var&gt; ÷ &lt;var&gt;D&lt;/var&gt;))&lt;sup&gt;&lt;var&gt;C&lt;/var&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, and for damage spells, the total damage done during the taper duration is &lt;var&gt;M&lt;/var&gt;&lt;var&gt;W&lt;/var&gt;&lt;var&gt;D&lt;/var&gt; ÷ (&lt;var&gt;C&lt;/var&gt; + 1).&lt;/p&gt;</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignRight|Qt::AlignTrailing|Qt::AlignVCenter</set>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="0" column="3">
        <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="baseCost">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>&lt;p&gt;The effect's base cost (to the caster's magicka, or to the enchanted item's charge). This is used as an input to a formula that calculates the final cost based on the caster's skill level, perks, and any other applicable factors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note that changing this value may not necessarily affect a spell's magicka cost, if the spell auto-calculates that cost. This is because spells recompute their cost at load time; if a mod changes the base cost of a spell's effects, without changing the spell itself, then nothing will force the spell to re-check the base costs and recalculate the overall magicka cost.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignRight|Qt::AlignTrailing|Qt::AlignVCenter</set>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="1" column="3">
        <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="skillUsageMult">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>A multiplier applied to the skill experience that the player gains when casting this effect.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignRight|Qt::AlignTrailing|Qt::AlignVCenter</set>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
      </layout>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox">
       <property name="title">
        <string>Flags</string>
       </property>
       <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_2">
        <item row="3" column="1">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagNoDuration">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>If checked, this effect applies instantaneously, and its duration can't be configured when attaching it to spells, potions, and so on.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>No Duration</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="2" column="1">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagNoDeathDispel">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>By default, magic effects are dispelled when their target dies. This option allows you to make the effect persist on the target even after death.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>No Death Dispel</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="0" column="0">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagHostile">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>This effect is treated as an attack, and is subject to being resisted by the target's Resist Value.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Hostile</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="1" column="0">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagDetrimental">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>&lt;p&gt;If checked, this effect will damage the Actor Value that it targets. If unchecked, this effect will buff the Actor Value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The word &quot;damage&quot; here means &quot;worsen,&quot; not &quot;reduce.&quot; A small number of Actor Values, such as MovementNoiseMult, are inverted such that &quot;damaging&quot; them &lt;em&gt;increases&lt;/em&gt; their value (i.e. you make more noise) and &quot;buffing&quot; them &lt;em&gt;decreases&lt;/em&gt; their value (i.e. you make less noise).&lt;/p&gt;</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Detrimental</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="4" column="0">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagSnapToNavmesh">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>If checked, the Aimed or Target Location point will be snapped to the nearest point on the Navmesh. This is primarily useful for summoned creatures, to ensure that they spawn somewhere they can actually move around in.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Snap to Navmesh</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="0" column="1">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagNoRecast">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>If checked, this effect can't be applied to a target if it's already active on that target; the effect must wear off or be dispelled before it can be applied to that target again.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>No Recast</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="4" column="1">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagNoHitEvent">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>If checked, this effect is stealthy: the target doesn't register a hit event when struck.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>No Hit Event</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="2" column="0">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagRecover">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>&lt;p&gt;If this is checked, then the effect acts as a buff or debuff: the target Actor Value's current and maximum values will be altered once when the effect begins, and those alterations will be undone when the effect expires.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this is unchecked, then the effect acts as damage or restoration over time: the target Actor Value's current value will be altered once per second until the effect expires, and the alterations will not be undone when the effect expires.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Recover</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="1" column="1">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagNoHitEffect">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>Disable visual effects that would otherwise play on the target of this effect.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>No Hit Effect</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="3" column="0">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagFXPersist">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>If checked, the visual effects applied to the target persist for the duration of the effect. If unchecked, they play only once, when the effect is first applied.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>FX Persist</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="0" column="2">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagNoMagnitude">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>If checked, this effect will not have a configurable magnitude, when attaching it to spells, potions, and so on.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>No Magnitude</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="1" column="2">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagNoArea">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>If checked, this effect will not have a configurable area (radius), when attaching it to spells, potions, and so on.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>No Area</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="2" column="2">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagPainless">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>If checked, the target of this effect won't cry out in pain even if the effect is hostile. If the target is the player, this checkbox also prevents the screen blur effect that appears when taking damage.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Painless</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="3" column="2">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagGory">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>Unused.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Gory Visuals</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="4" column="2">
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagHideInUI">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>&lt;p&gt;If checked, this effect is not displayed to the player in the Active Effects menu, and its description will be omitted from spells' auto-generated descriptions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If all Magic Effects attached to an Enchantment have this flag checked, then the enchanted equipment will appear unenchanted and, in the case of weapons, not display a charge bar on-screen. This is purely visual, however; the enchantment will still function as intended.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Hide in UI</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox_2">
       <property name="title">
        <string>Keywords</string>
       </property>
       <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout">
        <item>
         <widget class="QCheckBox" name="dispelOthersWithKeyword">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>If this is checked, then when this Magic Effect applies to a target, any Spells that are currently active on the target will be dispelled if any of their own effects have any of these keywords.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Dispel other effects with these keywords</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <widget class="DKFormListPane" name="keywords">
          <property name="showFormTypes">
           <bool>false</bool>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox_4">
       <property name="title">
        <string>Counter Effects</string>
       </property>
       <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_12">
        <item row="0" column="0">
         <widget class="DKFormListPane" name="counterEffects">
          <property name="maximumSize">
           <size>
            <width>16777215</width>
            <height>120</height>
           </size>
          </property>
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>Unused.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="showFormTypes">
           <bool>false</bool>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
   <item row="0" column="1" colspan="2">
    <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox_3">
     <property name="title">
      <string>Target Conditions</string>
     </property>
     <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_3">
      <item row="0" column="0">
       <widget class="DKConditionList" name="conditions">
        <property name="whatsThis">
         <string>&lt;p&gt;The effect can only be applied to targets that match these conditions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For spell effects, these are used in conjunction with conditions on the spell itself, to determine both whether and when the effect can apply to a given target. Refer to the notes in the spell-editing dialog for more information.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="1" column="1">
    <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="midCol">
     <item>
      <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_4">
       <item row="0" column="0">
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_18">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Menu Display Object:</string>
         </property>
         <property name="buddy">
          <cstring>menuDisplayObject</cstring>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="0" column="1">
        <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="menuDisplayObject">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>&lt;p&gt;The 3D model displayed for this effect in the Active Effects menu. This has to be a Static form.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reason why this has to be a Static form is not officially documented, but it may be because under the hood, the 3D models shown in the game's UI are actually references. Yeah, like, the things you place in the game world. The game just spawns a reference at &quot;nowhere,&quot; sets an &quot;I don't actually exist and everything should ignore me&quot; flag on it, and renders it into the UI. And references need base forms, don't they?&lt;/p&gt;</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
      </layout>
     </item>
