          <property name="text">
           <string>Detection Sound Level:</string>
          </property>
          <property name="buddy">
           <cstring>detectionSoundLevel</cstring>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="1" column="1">
         <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="soundCharge">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>For Fire and Forget spells, this sound plays when the player first presses the cast button down.</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="2" column="1">
         <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="soundReady">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>For Fire and Forget spells, this sound plays when the spell reaches its &quot;ready&quot; state, such that releasing the button will cast the spell.</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="3" column="1">
         <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="soundRelease">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>For Fire and Forget spells, this sound plays when the player releases the cast button and casts the spell (provided the spell is ready).</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="4" column="1">
         <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="soundCastLoop">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>For Concentration spells, this sound loops while the effect is being cast.</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="5" column="1">
         <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="soundOnHit">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>The sound that plays when this effect is applied to its target.</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item row="6" column="1">
         <widget class="QComboBox" name="detectionSoundLevel">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>The effect's loudness as perceived by NPC AI (with respect to stealth and detection).</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout_4">
       <item>
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_20">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Description:</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item>
        <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="description">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>&lt;p&gt;A description of this magic effect. This description will appear in the Active Effects menu, when the player is affected by this magic effect, and in the description of any Spell, Enchantment, Potion, or Scroll that has this effect and lacks a description of its own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This text field supports text replacement tags similar to those found in quest text. The text that gets substituted in will be displayed in bold. The available substitutions are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;dl&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;mag&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;The effect's magnitude. If the effect is flagged as having no magnitude, then nothing is displayed.&lt;/dd&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;dur&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;The effect's duration in seconds. If the effect is flagged as having no duration, then nothing is displayed.&lt;/dd&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;area&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;The effect's area (radius). If the effect is flagged as having no area, then nothing is displayed.&lt;/dd&gt;
   &lt;dt&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;global=EditorID&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;
      &lt;dd&gt;The current value of the Global with the given &lt;code&gt;EditorID&lt;/code&gt;. If no such global exists, then nothing is displayed. (Writing &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;global&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; has the same effect as failing to specify a valid global: nothing is displayed.)&lt;/dd&gt;
&lt;/dl&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It's possible to abuse text replacement to make arbitrary text bold: any text between angle brackets will be made bold, &lt;em&gt;but&lt;/em&gt; if that text contains &lt;code&gt;=&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;.&lt;/code&gt;, it will be cut off at the first such symbol. This is because text replacement uses the same syntax as in quests: &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Tag.Subtag=Parameter&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;: unrecognized tags are printed verbatim and in bold, but their subtags and parameters are discarded.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
      </layout>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="DKPapyrusBoundScriptListPane" name="scriptListPane"/>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
